				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				85,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add webview-view update and event forwarding handlers\n\nAdd two new SkyBridge capabilities for complete webview-view integration:\n\n1. `sky://webview/updateView` handler - Bridges Cocoon `view.title` / `view.description` / `view.badge` setter notifications to update the parked workbench `WebviewView`. Dispatches `cel:webview:updateView` for observers.\n\n2. Workbench → Extension event forwarding - Inside the view registration block, subscribe to workbench events and forward them to Cocoon:\n   - `WebviewView.webview.onDidReceivedMessage` → `webview.message` notification\n   - `WebviewView.onDidChangeVisibility` → `webview.viewState` notification\n   - `WebviewView.onDispose` → `webview.dispose` notification AND cleanup of `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS__` registry\n\nThis completes the webview-view lifecycle: register → resolve → set-html → update-metadata → communicate → dispose.",
			"SHA": "c708338bda9738970b433105895f09edff3498f1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T21:02:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				85,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add webview-view set-html and postMessage handlers\n\nAdd two new SkyBridge handlers to complete the webview-view integration path:\n\n1. `sky://webview/set-html` - When a Cocoon-side `resolveWebviewView` callback sets `view.webview.html`, Mountain re-emits the `webview.setHtml` notification. This handler looks up the parked workbench `WebviewView` (registered via prior `sky://webview/registerView`) by viewId from `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS__` and applies the HTML to its real `webview.html` setter so the panel paints. Also dispatches `cel:webview:set-html` DOM event for Sky-side observers.\n\n2. `sky://webview/postMessage` - When an extension calls `view.webview.postMessage(msg)`, the notification is forwarded to this handler. It dispatches `cel:webview:post-message` and forwards the message to the parked workbench view's webview when a viewId match exists.\n\nBoth handlers integrate with the parked `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS__` registry created during view registration, completing the full lifecycle: register → resolve (set-html) → communicate (postMessage) → unregister.",
			"SHA": "40ca326cd1e83be0b745fa0ba5fe8c9d62dd0a69"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T20:52:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				85,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add webview view provider registration handlers\n\nAdd two new SkyBridge handlers to support VS Code extension webview views (sidebar/panel content):\n\n1. `sky://webview/registerView` - Registers viewIds with the workbench's `IWebviewViewService`. When the workbench calls `resolve(webview, ct)`, the handler posts a `webview.resolveView` reverse-RPC through Mountain to trigger the extension's `resolveWebviewView` callback. The workbench view is parked in `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS__` for future correlation with `sky://webview/set-html`.\n\n2. `sky://webview/unregisterView` - Cleans up the registry on extension disposal.\n\nThis enables extensions like GitLens, Explorer, and other activity-bar panels to render their webview content when clicked, completing the webview integration path alongside existing custom editor support.",
			"SHA": "6c9a73258557dad682efdf2dd2c12f30dd814320"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T19:53:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				85,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add debug DAP message and custom editor save event handlers\n\nAdd two new SkyBridge handlers to bridge VS Code workbench services:\n\n1. `sky://debug/dap-message` - Forwards parsed DAP frames from Mountain's spawned debug-adapter stdout into a `cel:debug:dap-message` DOM event. This enables a future RawDebugSession shim to subscribe and correlate responses by `request_seq` without re-implementing DAP framing.\n\n2. `sky://customEditor/saved` - Dispatches `cel:customEditor:saved` after Mountain's `OnSaveCustomDocument` reverse-RPC succeeds. While the workbench's dirty indicator updates via `IFileService.writeFile`, observers like gitlens diff overlays listen for this explicit \"extension save callback completed\" signal.\n\nBoth handlers integrate with the existing custom event system, extending the bridge pattern established by recent SCM and debug session lifecycle handlers.",
			"SHA": "4a742ea282dacf7da6949b967b01e1b5d1e1ec70"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T14:46:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				85,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add webview post-message bridge for extension communication\n\nAdd a new handler for `sky://webview/post-message` that dispatches `cel:webview:post-message` custom events to the renderer. This bridges the raw extension `postMessage` path from Cocoon (gRPC `OnDidReceiveMessage` + `PostWebviewMessage`) which carries the `{ handle, message }` shape, distinct from the existing `sky://webview/message` handler that uses the workbench-RPC `{ panelId, method, params }` shape.\n\nThis enables extension-hosted code to communicate back to the Sky webview UI components through the established custom event system.",
			"SHA": "f0fabc61973c57267f70deed92d8282649881958"
		}
	],
